my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
Hello world
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{a appends text after cursor position},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/insert_append_a`

Tests that the **a** command enters insert mode with the cursor positioned
after the current character, so typed text is appended after the cursor.

**Keys:** `a`, type `XY`, `Escape`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "Hello world"
- Cursor at column 0 on 'H'

**after_append.png**
- Line reads "HXYello world" (XY inserted between H and e)
- Cursor on 'e' (moved back one after Escape)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->key('a');
        $ctx->type('XY');
        $ctx->key('Escape');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_append');
    },
}
